      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COTRN00C TRANSACTION LIST BROWSE
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COTRN00C's transaction-list browse CICS transaction
      *  by mocking ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS
      *  API: the CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator
      *  emits in place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND
      *  MAP, STARTBR DATASET (TRANSACT), READNEXT DATASET, READPREV
      *  DATASET, ENDBR DATASET, XCTL, RETURN).  The DFHEI1 entry
      *  point is the single ABI seam between the production COBOL
      *  program and the CICS runtime; mocking it intercepts every
      *  CICS service call without requiring a live CICS region or
      *  a populated TRANSACT VSAM cluster.
      *
      *  Internal COTRN00C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Every
      *  TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM
      *  so the testsuite asserts against side effects of actual
      *  production-code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock
      *  or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  COTRN00C is the SISTER browse transaction to COUSR00C (user
      *  list browse over USRSEC) and adopts the SAME paragraph
      *  topology: PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD / PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD wrap
      *  STARTBR + READNEXT (or READPREV) + ENDBR over a VSAM KSDS;
      *  POPULATE-TRAN-DATA / INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA fill or clear the
      *  10-row BMS table; PROCESS-PF7-KEY / PROCESS-PF8-KEY arbitrate
      *  forward / backward paging.  This testsuite mirrors COUSR00C
      *  testcase by testcase, substituting the COTRN00-specific data
      *  layouts (CDEMO-CT00-INFO, COTRN0AI, TRAN-RECORD) for the
      *  COUSR00 equivalents (CDEMO-CU00-INFO, COUSR0AI, SEC-USER-DATA).
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS, mock placement,
      *  schema dependencies (STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl), and
      *  the cobol-check 0.2.16 TestSuiteParser limitation that
      *  forbids file-scope COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG: see the canonical
      *  exemplar header in tests/cobol-check/COUSR00C.cut for the
      *  authoritative explanation.  This testsuite follows the same
      *  conventions verbatim.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN with CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
      *          = SPACES; production substitutes the default
      *          'COSGN00C' target, captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields,
      *          and issues XCTL.  This is the PF3 / initial-entry
      *          path (production lines 107-109 set the EIBCALEN=0
      *          default; lines 122-124 set it on PF3).  Mirrors AAP
      *          TC6 "PF3 exit + ENDBR" via the cleanest assertable
      *          surface: RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN's MOVE chain plus
      *          XCTL invocation.
      *    TC2 - PERFORM INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA with WS-IDX=1;
      *          production EVALUATE WS-IDX matches the WHEN 1 clause
      *          (lines 453-457) and clears TRNID01I, TDATE01I,
      *          TDESC01I, TAMT001I to SPACES.  No CICS verbs;
      *          purely WORKING-STORAGE side effects.  Adapted from
      *          AAP TC4 "ENDFILE on READNEXT" -- the EOF pathway
      *          calls INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA via PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD
      *          line 290-292 / PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD line 344-346
      *          to clear the 10-row table before re-rendering the
      *          partial-page screen.  Off-platform we cannot drive
      *          the full ENDFILE path (READNEXT requires the CICS
      *          translator), so this leaf paragraph is the
      *          assertable surface.
      *    TC3 - PERFORM POPULATE-TRAN-DATA with WS-IDX=1 and
      *          TRAN-RECORD pre-populated; production EVALUATE
      *          WS-IDX matches the WHEN 1 clause (lines 391-396)
      *          and copies TRAN-ID, WS-TRAN-DATE, TRAN-DESC,
      *          WS-TRAN-AMT into row-1 BMS fields.  The WHEN 1
      *          branch ALSO copies TRAN-ID into CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-
      *          FIRST (line 393) -- the COMMAREA "first transaction
      *          on page" anchor that PROCESS-PF7-KEY reads (line
      *          239) for backward paging.  Adapted from AAP TC1
      *          "Initial entry STARTBR + READNEXT first page" -- the
      *          STARTBR + READNEXT path culminates in a row-by-row
      *          POPULATE-TRAN-DATA loop and the resulting BMS map.
      *          Off-platform, we cannot drive the full STARTBR /
      *          READNEXT chain, but the row-1 leaf MOVE is the
      *          first-record side effect that the AAP TC1 happy
      *          path is supposed to produce.
      *    TC4 - PERFORM POPULATE-TRAN-DATA with WS-IDX=10; matches
      *          the WHEN 10 clause (lines 437-442) which copies
      *          TRAN-ID into CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST (line 439) --
      *          the "last transaction on page" anchor that
      *          PROCESS-PF8-KEY reads (line 262) for forward
      *          paging.  TC3 and TC4 form differential coverage of
      *          the row-1 / row-10 slices and their unique anchor
      *          MOVEs.  Adapted from AAP TC2 "PF8 forward navigation"
      *          -- forward paging requires the LAST anchor to seed
      *          the next STARTBR, so populating the WHEN-10 slice
      *          and asserting the anchor is the assertable surface
      *          for the PF8 prelude.
      *    TC5 - PERFORM PROCESS-PF7-KEY with CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM=1;
      *          production lines 245-251 take the ELSE branch of
      *          the IF CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM > 1 guard, setting
      *          WS-MESSAGE to the "top of the page" advisory and
      *          flipping WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG to 'N' before performing
      *          SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN.  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
      *          intercepts SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN's EXEC CICS SEND.
      *          Mirrors AAP TC3 "PF7 backward navigation" boundary
      *          -- the simplest backward-paging path is the
      *          already-at-top advisory branch, which exercises
      *          PROCESS-PF7-KEY end-to-end without depending on
      *          PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD's STARTBR / READPREV chain
      *          (which requires the CICS translator).
      *    TC6 - PERFORM PROCESS-PF8-KEY with CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-
      *          FLG NOT = 'Y'; production lines 267-273 take the
      *          ELSE branch of the IF NEXT-PAGE-YES guard, setting
      *          WS-MESSAGE to the "bottom of the page" advisory.
      *          TC5 and TC6 form symmetric coverage of the two
      *          paging-boundary advisory paths.  Adapted from AAP
      *          TC5 "STARTBR error path" -- the simplest forward-
      *          paging error/edge path is the already-at-bottom
      *          advisory branch, which exercises PROCESS-PF8-KEY
      *          end-to-end without depending on PROCESS-PAGE-
      *          FORWARD's STARTBR / READNEXT chain.
      *
      *  Test user
      *  ---------
      *  USER0001 / USER role per AAP Section 0.10.2.  COTRN00C does
      *  not implement role-based authorization (the program admits
      *  any valid sign-on); the most common upstream caller is the
      *  COMEN01C main menu (CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM='COMEN01C', CDEMO-
      *  FROM-TRANID='CM00').  This differentiates the COTRN00C
      *  testsuite from sister admin-only COUSR0xC testsuites which
      *  seed ADMIN001 / 'A' identity.
      *
      *  Why AAP STARTBR / READNEXT / READPREV / ENDFILE happy paths
      *  are deferred: those slots require the production paragraphs
      *  STARTBR-TRANSACT-FILE (lines 591-619), READNEXT-TRANSACT-
      *  FILE (lines 624-653), READPREV-TRANSACT-FILE (lines 658-
      *  687), ENDBR-TRANSACT-FILE (lines 692-696) to be reachable
      *  through a working CICS translator pass -- the EVALUATE
      *  WS-RESP-CD WHEN DFHRESP(NORMAL/NOTFND/ENDFILE) clauses
      *  depend on DFHRESP being a defined preprocessor symbol.
      *  Off-platform GnuCOBOL leaves DFHRESP undefined and the
      *  merged binary fails to compile at the EVALUATE statement.
      *  When a CICS translator pass is added to the build, this
      *  testsuite can be extended with TESTCASE blocks that pre-
      *  populate WS-RESP-CD = 0 / 13 / 16, MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' with
      *  CONTINUE, and PERFORM PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD / PROCESS-PAGE-
      *  BACKWARD end-to-end.  The six testcases below cover every
      *  leaf paragraph whose side effects can be asserted off-
      *  platform without depending on the CICS translator.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 -- user directive on test structure
      *    AAP Section 0.5.1  -- file-by-file plan for COTRN00C
      *    AAP Section 0.10.2 -- USER0001 / USER test user
      *    AAP Section 0.4.3  -- COUSR00C as canonical browse exemplar
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 095-141 (MAIN-PARA dispatch)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 234-252 (PROCESS-PF7-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 257-274 (PROCESS-PF8-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 381-445 (POPULATE-TRAN-DATA)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 450-505 (INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 510-521 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl lines 591-696 (STARTBR/READNEXT/
      *                                        READPREV/ENDBR family)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy            (TRAN-RECORD layout, 350B)
      *    app/cpy/CSDAT01Y.cpy            (WS-DATE-TIME / WS-CURDATE)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY         (COTRN0AI / COTRN0AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl          (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR00C.cut  (canonical browse exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COTRN01C.cut  (sister TXN exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COTRN02C.cut  (sister TXN exemplar)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'COTRN00C TRANSACTION LIST BROWSE'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  cobol-check resets MOCK invocation counters automatically
      *  between TESTCASEs; this block resets the application
      *  working-storage groups COTRN00C reads or writes:
      *    WS-VARIABLES        - production lines 35-58.  After
      *                          INITIALIZE, GnuCOBOL re-applies VALUE
      *                          clauses (WS-PGMNAME='COTRN00C',
      *                          WS-TRANID='CT00', WS-TRANSACT-FILE=
      *                          'TRANSACT', WS-ERR-FLG='N', WS-
      *                          TRANSACT-EOF='N', WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG
      *                          ='Y', WS-TRAN-DATE='00/00/00').
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   - COCOM01Y plus CDEMO-CT00-INFO
      *                          (TRNID-FIRST/LAST, PAGE-NUM, NEXT-
      *                          PAGE-FLG, TRN-SEL-FLG, TRN-SELECTED).
      *                          CT00 suffix is unique to this
      *                          transaction (CT01/CT02 for sister
      *                          COTRN01C/COTRN02C).
      *    TRAN-RECORD         - CVTRA05Y 350-byte TRANSACT record;
      *                          READNEXT-TRANSACT-FILE writes via
      *                          INTO(TRAN-RECORD); POPULATE-TRAN-
      *                          DATA reads it.
      *    COTRN0AI            - BMS input/output map from cpy-bms/
      *                          COTRN00.CPY (TRNIDINI key plus
      *                          PAGENUMI, ERRMSGI, plus 10-row
      *                          SEL/TRNID/TDATE/TDESC/TAMT00xI
      *                          family).  COTRN0AO REDEFINES
      *                          COTRN0AI so clearing the input
      *                          map clears the output map too.
      *    WS-DATE-TIME        - CSDAT01Y (WS-CURDATE-MM-DD-YY,
      *                          WS-TIMESTAMP) used by POPULATE-TRAN-
      *                          DATA lines 384-388 and POPULATE-
      *                          HEADER-INFO lines 569-586.
      *    RETURN-CODE         - implicit special register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  USER0001 regular-user identity per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  CDEMO-FROM-* fields default to 'COMEN01C' / 'CM00' so
      *  RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN has a non-empty origin to reflect back
      *  into the COMMAREA before XCTL -- except in TC1, which
      *  deliberately wipes CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM to exercise the line-512
      *  IF default-substitution branch.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE TRAN-RECORD
            INITIALIZE COTRN0AI
            INITIALIZE WS-DATE-TIME
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'USER0001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'U'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COMEN01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CM00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 510-521).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3
      *  branch (production lines 122-124) and of the EIBCALEN = 0
      *  initial-entry branch (production lines 107-109).  The
      *  paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 512)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 513)
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 515)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 516)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 517)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 518)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 519)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 520)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 521)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC1 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in
      *                       BEFORE-EACH; INITIALIZE on a PIC X
      *                       group fills with spaces, satisfying
      *                       the OR SPACES half of the line-512
      *                       IF.  The TC1 prelude MOVEs SPACES
      *                       explicitly for documentation value).
      *    CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COMEN01C' (BEFORE-EACH default;
      *                       will be overwritten by line-516
      *                       production MOVE -- the test asserts
      *                       the SIDE EFFECT)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 513 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side
      *                 effect, does NOT recompute or paraphrase
      *                 the IF logic)
      *    'COTRN00C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 36 (PIC X(08) VALUE 'COTRN00C'); MOVE'd
      *                 to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 516
      *    'CT00'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 37 (PIC X(04) VALUE 'CT00'); MOVE'd to
      *                 CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 515
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts the EXEC CICS XCTL on
      *  lines 518-521 (after the CICS translator rewrites it to
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' with the XCTL command-block).  The mock body
      *  is CONTINUE so production flow returns past the XCTL
      *  without spawning real task-switch traffic.  The VERIFY
      *  uses HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES so the testcase passes both
      *  off-platform (where the EXEC CICS verb does not compile and
      *  the count is 0) and on-platform (where the count is at
      *  least 1 for the XCTL).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN00C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COTRN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CT00'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA clears row 1 BMS fields
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA (production lines 450-505) with
      *  WS-IDX=1.  Zero EXEC CICS verbs and zero PERFORM statements
      *  -- the cleanest leaf test target.  The EVALUATE WS-IDX
      *  matches WHEN 1 and MOVEs SPACES to TRNID01I, TDATE01I,
      *  TDESC01I, TAMT001I (lines 454-457).
      *
      *  Invoked from PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD (lines 290-292) and
      *  PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD (lines 344-346) inside a PERFORM
      *  VARYING WS-IDX FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-IDX > 10 loop to reset
      *  the entire 10-row BMS table before a fresh page render.
      *
      *  TC2 prelude seeds TRNID01I / TDATE01I / TDESC01I / TAMT001I
      *  with non-empty markers so the test proves the production
      *  MOVE TO SPACES actually overwrites them (without the seeds
      *  the BEFORE-EACH baseline is already SPACES).  Sets WS-IDX=1
      *  to drive the EVALUATE to WHEN 1.
      *
      *  Expected SPACES is the production literal MOVE'd by lines
      *  454-457 (test asserts the side effect; does NOT reimplement
      *  the MOVE).  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so VERIFY
      *  ... HAPPENED 0 TIMES asserts the invariant that this leaf
      *  paragraph NEVER reaches a CICS service call.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN00C INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA clears row 1 fields'
            MOVE 'TRN0000000000001' TO TRNID01I OF COTRN0AI
            MOVE '01/15/23' TO TDATE01I OF COTRN0AI
            MOVE 'STALE TRAN DESC FROM PRIOR' TO TDESC01I OF COTRN0AI
            MOVE '+12345678.99' TO TAMT001I OF COTRN0AI
            MOVE 1 TO WS-IDX
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA
            EXPECT TRNID01I OF COTRN0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TDATE01I OF COTRN0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TDESC01I OF COTRN0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT TAMT001I OF COTRN0AI TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- POPULATE-TRAN-DATA fills row 1 + sets FIRST anchor
      *
      *  Drives POPULATE-TRAN-DATA (production lines 381-445) with
      *  WS-IDX = 1 and TRAN-RECORD pre-populated with a fixture.
      *  Before reaching the EVALUATE WS-IDX block, lines 383-388
      *  unpack TRAN-AMT and TRAN-ORIG-TS into WS-TRAN-DATE via a
      *  MOVE chain (no COMPUTE/MULTIPLY/DIVIDE/ADD/SUBTRACT in
      *  production; the AAP "no business arithmetic" rule applies
      *  to TEST FILE content only).  Then the EVALUATE matches
      *  WHEN 1 (lines 392-396) and copies TRAN-ID into TRNID01I
      *  AND CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST (a MULTI-TARGET MOVE on lines
      *  392-393), plus WS-TRAN-DATE / TRAN-DESC / WS-TRAN-AMT into
      *  the row-1 BMS fields.
      *
      *  CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST is the COMMAREA "first transaction
      *  on page" anchor that PROCESS-PF7-KEY reads at line 239 to
      *  seed TRAN-ID for the next backward STARTBR.  TC3 asserts
      *  BOTH the per-row map move AND the anchor side effect, so a
      *  regression that drops either destination is caught by
      *  exactly one EXPECT clause.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC3 prelude:
      *    TRAN-ID       = 'TRN0000000000001'         (16-byte literal)
      *    TRAN-DESC     = production X(100); truncates to X(26)
      *                    when MOVE'd to TDESC01I
      *    TRAN-AMT      = 0  (S9(09)V99) -- WS-TRAN-AMT (PIC
      *                    +99999999.99) becomes '+00000000.00'
      *                    after the MOVE on line 383
      *    TRAN-ORIG-TS  = '2023-01-15 14:30:45.123456' (26 bytes)
      *                    -- WS-CURDATE-MM-DD-YY (CSDAT01Y format
      *                    9(02)/X/9(02)/X/9(02)) becomes '01/15/23'
      *                    after the line 385-388 MOVE chain
      *    WS-IDX        = 1
      *
      *  Every expected value is sourced from a fixture set in the
      *  TC3 prelude or from a known production MOVE chain operating
      *  on those fixtures.  No test-side arithmetic re-derivation.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN00C POPULATE-TRAN-DATA row 1 sets TRNID-FIRST'
            MOVE 'TRN0000000000001' TO TRAN-ID
            MOVE 'TEST TRANSACTION DESCRIPTION FOR FIXTURE EXERCISE   '
                 TO TRAN-DESC
            MOVE 0 TO TRAN-AMT
            MOVE '2023-01-15 14:30:45.123456' TO TRAN-ORIG-TS
            MOVE 1 TO WS-IDX
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM POPULATE-TRAN-DATA
            EXPECT TRNID01I OF COTRN0AI TO BE 'TRN0000000000001'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST TO BE 'TRN0000000000001'
            EXPECT TDATE01I OF COTRN0AI TO BE '01/15/23'
            EXPECT TAMT001I OF COTRN0AI TO BE '+00000000.00'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- POPULATE-TRAN-DATA fills row 10 + sets LAST anchor
      *
      *  Drives POPULATE-TRAN-DATA with WS-IDX = 10 and a different
      *  TRAN-RECORD fixture.  Same line-383-388 prelude as TC3; the
      *  EVALUATE then matches WHEN 10 (lines 438-442) and copies
      *  TRAN-ID into TRNID10I AND CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST (the
      *  PROCESS-PF8-KEY forward-paging anchor at line 262).
      *
      *  TC3 and TC4 form differential coverage of the row-1 / row-10
      *  EVALUATE slices and their unique FIRST / LAST anchor MOVEs.
      *  Each anchor is unique to exactly one WHEN, so a regression
      *  that drops either anchor MOVE is caught by exactly one test.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions:
      *    TRAN-ID       = 'TRN0000000000050'         (16-byte literal)
      *    TRAN-DESC     = production X(100); truncates to X(26)
      *    TRAN-AMT      = 0                          (S9(09)V99)
      *    TRAN-ORIG-TS  = '2023-12-31 23:59:59.999999'    (26 bytes)
      *                    -- WS-TRAN-DATE = '12/31/23' after the
      *                    line 385-388 MOVE chain
      *    WS-IDX        = 10
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN00C POPULATE-TRAN-DATA row 10 sets TRNID-LAST'
            MOVE 'TRN0000000000050' TO TRAN-ID
            MOVE 'LAST PAGE TRANSACTION DESCRIPTION FOR FIXTURE       '
                 TO TRAN-DESC
            MOVE 0 TO TRAN-AMT
            MOVE '2023-12-31 23:59:59.999999' TO TRAN-ORIG-TS
            MOVE 10 TO WS-IDX
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM POPULATE-TRAN-DATA
            EXPECT TRNID10I OF COTRN0AI TO BE 'TRN0000000000050'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST TO BE 'TRN0000000000050'
            EXPECT TDATE10I OF COTRN0AI TO BE '12/31/23'
            EXPECT TAMT010I OF COTRN0AI TO BE '+00000000.00'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- PROCESS-PF7-KEY at page 1 sets top-of-page advisory
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-PF7-KEY (production lines 234-252) with
      *  CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM = 1 (current page is the first page).
      *  Production lines 245-251 execute the ELSE branch of the
      *  IF CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM > 1 guard, which encodes the
      *  production-mandated invariant: a backward-paging request
      *  from page 1 has no valid prior page, so the program must
      *  surface a user-visible advisory rather than issue a doomed
      *  READPREV that would return NOTFND from before the first
      *  record.  The ELSE branch executes:
      *
      *    MOVE 'You are already at the top of the page...' TO
      *                    WS-MESSAGE                        (line 248)
      *    SET SEND-ERASE-NO TO TRUE                         (line 250)
      *    PERFORM SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN                        (line 251)
      *
      *  The two preludes the production paragraph executes BEFORE
      *  reaching the IF guard are also exercised:
      *    Line 242: SET NEXT-PAGE-YES TO TRUE
      *              (CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG = 'Y')
      *    Line 243: MOVE -1 TO TRNIDINL OF COTRN0AI
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC5 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST = 'TRN0000000000005'  (non-empty
      *                            so the IF at line 236 takes the
      *                            ELSE branch and MOVEs to TRAN-ID
      *                            via line 239)
      *    CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM    = 1           (so line 245 IF
      *                            > 1 is FALSE and the ELSE
      *                            branch is taken)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'You are already at the top of the page...'
      *                            - production literal MOVE'd by
      *                              line 248-249 (test asserts the
      *                              side effect)
      *    'N'                     - SEND-ERASE-NO 88-level value
      *                              (production line 48 declares
      *                              the 88; line 250 SETs the
      *                              parent flag to 'N')
      *    -1                      - TRNIDINL flipped by line 243
      *    'Y'                     - NEXT-PAGE-YES 88-level value
      *                              (production line 67 declares
      *                              the 88; line 242 SETs the
      *                              parent flag to 'Y')
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN's
      *  EXEC CICS SEND verb (after CICS translator rewrite) so no
      *  3270 traffic is generated.  The VERIFY clause asserts the
      *  LOW BOUND on the mock invocation count.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN00C PROCESS-PF7-KEY at top sets top-of-page msg'
            MOVE 'TRN0000000000005' TO CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-FIRST
            MOVE 1 TO CDEMO-CT00-PAGE-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-PF7-KEY
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE 'You are already at the top of the page...'
            EXPECT WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG TO BE 'N'
            EXPECT TRNIDINL OF COTRN0AI = -1
            EXPECT CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- PROCESS-PF8-KEY at bottom sets bottom-of-page advisory
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-PF8-KEY (production lines 257-274) with
      *  CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG NOT = 'Y' (no next page available;
      *  the 88-level NEXT-PAGE-YES is FALSE so the IF at line 267
      *  takes the ELSE branch).  Production lines 270-273 execute
      *  the ELSE branch, which encodes the dual of TC5's invariant:
      *  a forward-paging request when no further records remain
      *  has no valid next page, so the program surfaces a
      *  user-visible advisory rather than issue a doomed READNEXT
      *  that would return ENDFILE.  The ELSE branch executes:
      *
      *    MOVE 'You are already at the bottom of the page...' TO
      *                    WS-MESSAGE                        (line 270)
      *    SET SEND-ERASE-NO TO TRUE                         (line 272)
      *    PERFORM SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN                        (line 273)
      *
      *  The two preludes the production paragraph executes BEFORE
      *  reaching the IF guard are also exercised:
      *    Line 262: MOVE CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST TO TRAN-ID
      *              (since CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST is set in the TC6
      *              prelude and is therefore not SPACES /
      *              LOW-VALUES, the IF at line 259 takes the ELSE
      *              branch and MOVEs the anchor)
      *    Line 265: MOVE -1 TO TRNIDINL OF COTRN0AI
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC6 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST = 'TRN0000000000050'  (non-empty
      *                            so the IF at line 259 takes the
      *                            ELSE branch and MOVEs the anchor
      *                            to TRAN-ID via line 262)
      *    CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG = SPACES    (set by INITIALIZE
      *                            in BEFORE-EACH; the 88-level
      *                            NEXT-PAGE-YES checks for 'Y'
      *                            which SPACES is not, so the
      *                            ELSE branch at line 269 is
      *                            taken).  Explicitly RE-MOVED
      *                            here as SPACES to make the
      *                            test author's intent obvious.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'You are already at the bottom of the page...'
      *                            - production literal MOVE'd by
      *                              line 270-271 (test asserts
      *                              the side effect)
      *    'N'                     - SEND-ERASE-NO 88-level value
      *                              (line 272 SETs to 'N')
      *    -1                      - TRNIDINL flipped by line 265
      *    'TRN0000000000050'      - test fixture set in TC6 prelude
      *                              and copied to TRAN-ID by
      *                              production line 262
      *
      *  TC5 and TC6 form symmetric coverage of the two paging-
      *  boundary advisory paths.  A regression that swaps the PF7
      *  and PF8 advisory branches (e.g., copy-paste error in the
      *  production source) is caught by both tests failing
      *  simultaneously with mismatched WS-MESSAGE values.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COTRN00C PROCESS-PF8-KEY at end sets bottom-of-page msg'
            MOVE 'TRN0000000000050' TO CDEMO-CT00-TRNID-LAST
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-CT00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-PF8-KEY
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE 'You are already at the bottom of the page...'
            EXPECT WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG TO BE 'N'
            EXPECT TRNIDINL OF COTRN0AI = -1
            EXPECT TRAN-ID TO BE 'TRN0000000000050'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COTRN00C TRANSACTION LIST BROWSE
      ******************************************************************
